+// Square a box's top two corners in the rounding shaders without touching the
+// quad: the shader carves its arcs at the corners of the box it is handed as
+// topLeft/fullSize, so pushing that box's top edge up by twice the radius puts
+// the two top arcs above the quad — nothing of them is drawn — while the two
+// bottom arcs stay exactly where they were. Applied BEFORE the output transform,
+// so "up" is the window's top on any rotation. (Used by windows tagged
+// `square-top`: a titlebar decoration continuing the frame flat across the seam.)
+static CBox squareTopRoundingBox(CBox box, float radius) {
+    box.y -= 2.F * radius;
+    box.h += 2.F * radius;
+    return box;
+}
